<%#
  Key Bindings Section (issue #1003)

  The entire bottom section of every action Property Inspector. Since the
  plugin-global settings moved to the dedicated settings window (#992, #993),
  all that remains per-action is the action's own key bindings — genuinely
  contextual, because each PI shows only its own category out of the full
  catalog — plus the link out to everything else.

  Owning the header, the accordion and the empty state in ONE partial keeps the
  25 PIs that have bindings and the 10 that do not consistent by construction,
  instead of by 35 copies of the same markup.

  Parameters:
    - keyBindings (Array, optional) — rows to render, in the shape
      `global-key-bindings` expects: { id, label, default, setting, class? }.
      Omit it (or pass an empty array) for an action with no bindings; the
      section then says so rather than rendering an empty accordion.
    - hidden (Boolean, optional) — start the bindings wrapper hidden so the PI
      can reveal it per mode (Fuel Service does this). The section HEADER stays
      visible either way, so the link to the settings window never disappears.

  The wrapper's `key-bindings-section` id is defined here and nowhere else —
  PI scripts toggle it by that id.

  NOTE: the accordion title inside `global-key-bindings` must stay exactly
  "Related Key Bindings" — `ird-binding-status` pins that literal
  (KEY_BINDINGS_ACCORDION_ID) to open and scroll the accordion from its
  "set it here" link, and `accordion.ejs` derives data-accordion-id from the
  title. Retitling it breaks that link and the _accordionState key.
  (EJS comment so this documentation is never emitted into the HTML.)
%>
<%- include('section-header', { title: 'Key Bindings', openSettings: true }) %>

<div id="key-bindings-section"<% if (locals.hidden) { %> class="hidden"<% } %>>
<% if (locals.keyBindings && keyBindings.length) { %>
<%- include('global-key-bindings', { keyBindings: keyBindings }) %>
<% } else { %>
<div class="ird-supporting-text">This action has no key bindings.</div>
<% } %>
</div>
